author ai
group features/gui
note The human, back from the agent's session, at the moment the status line says replies arrived but the green boxes are spread over the tours and files they commented on. Goal: understanding a change takes less friction than in an editor. Without this feature the human reopens each tour and file they remember commenting on and scrolls for green boxes, and a comment on code outside every tour is found only by remembering its file. A list of comments that navigates on click was the Comments view prototyped for add-comment; it showed where comments are but kept each reply away from the code it answers, so the count walks instead: each click goes to the next answered comment in id order, through the selection so back and forward return; a step comment selects its step in the Tour view, a tour comment opens its tour, a code comment opens its file in the Source view with its lines selected. With nothing answered it walks the open ones, so before starting the agent the human can reread what they asked. Comments are keyed by tour name and file path, and tour-rename and file moves do not carry them: in the GUI scenario 'comments', after 'tour-rename startup boot' the step comment on startup had no view to draw in. Such a comment shows in a box under the count when the walk reaches it, marked '(tour gone)' or '(file gone)', with its withdraw or dismiss and a close button, so the human can still read and remove it. Why comments exist is in feature-add-comment.

